# Local tooling, never part of the app or the deploy.
#
# .tools holds the portable Node runtime that `tools/bootstrap-node.py`
# downloads, the dev-only Lighthouse copy, the axe-core audit script, and the
# raw measurement output (heap snapshots, logs, scratch). The app itself has
# zero dependencies and the repository stays that way: nothing here is required
# to run or deploy the site.
.tools/

# Deployment build output (tools/build-site.py). Regenerable, never committed:
# `dist/` is the public copy, `dist-site/` the generated worker, and the
# manifest names both.
dist/
dist-site/
deploy.site.json
# Measurement scratch output that is large and regenerable.
*.heapsnapshot
# Local tool state: wrangler's workerd cache and Python bytecode from the
# helper scripts. Neither is part of the app or the deploy.
.wrangler/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
# Editor / AI-tool state that must never be part of the app or the deploy:
# Kiro's settings tree and the local deploy helper's project marker. Both are
# machine-local tool configuration, not project files - see tools/build-site.py,
# which already skips them when assembling dist/.
.kiro/
.freebuff/
# Throwaway browser profiles from the measurement tools (tools/cdp.js) and the
# ad-hoc `--user-data-dir=./cdp-probe-XXXX` probes. These are complete Chrome
# profiles - Cookies, Login Data, History, crash dumps, session logs - and must
# never be published. tools/cdp.js now creates them under the system temp
# directory; the patterns stay as a backstop for a probe run by hand.
cdp-probe-*/
singularity-cdp-*/

# Raw output from the measurement tools: browser/test run logs and stderr
# captures. Regenerable scratch, never project content.
*.log
*.err
